From 033ad9b8c9729ae9155fa61a1b958411e48f5f26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:04:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] eip155: ask every RPC for a failed send's hash, for two
 blocks if it timed out

The lookup after a failed send went through the fallback layer, which
takes the first answer, and null counts as one. A node that had not
seen the transaction could answer first while the other held it, so a
mined settlement was still reported as failed, with an empty hash.

Each RPC is now asked on its own, and any that knows the transaction
settles it. A send that timed out may have reached a node that alone
holds the transaction until it is mined, so that search lasts two of
Hemi's blocks. A send that was answered is looked up once.

The hash of a send that failed is now logged in both cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
